    <string name="method_idea_title">The idea: 80/20</string>
    <string name="method_idea_body">As much result as possible in as little time as possible. No long programs with five sets per exercise, but two sets per exercise that really count. Short, heavy and measurable.</string>
    <string name="method_sets_title">Two sets, both to failure</string>
    <string name="method_sets_body">Per exercise you do two sets straight after each other: heavy, then light. You stop only when no clean rep is left. The targets are aims, not orders: the reps follow from the weight.</string>
    <string name="method_plan_title">Plan on weight, not on reps</string>
    <string name="method_plan_body">After each exercise you set the weight for next time; the app suggests it per set. Within the margin (target ± 1): keep the weight and aim for one more rep. More reps: too light, one step heavier. Fewer reps: too heavy, one step lighter. A step depends on the material: bar and plates, pin stack, cable or dumbbells. The app only suggests weights you can actually load.</string>
    <string name="method_bw_title">Bodyweight and reps-only exercises</string>
    <string name="method_bw_body">Pull-ups and dips are planned with extra weight (+) or assistance (−). For exercises without weight the goal is simply more reps than last time.</string>
    <string name="method_go_title">Warm-up and GO</string>
    <string name="method_go_body">Warm-up sets are free and do not count. Only when you press GO does the exercise really start; the app then measures how long you train and how long switching takes.</string>
    <string name="method_week_title">A week plan instead of a timetable</string>
    <string name="method_week_body">Life is chaotic. A week plan says how often per week you want to train and which schemas you alternate. The app looks at what you already did this week and suggests what makes sense today. Skipping a day is fine; the plan moves along.</string>
    <string name="method_progress_title">Progress</string>
    <string name="method_progress_body">Records (best estimated 1RM on the heavy set), charts per exercise and a heatmap of your body show where your volume and progress are.</string>
    <string name="method_safety_title">Safety</string>
    <string name="method_safety_body">Training to failure is intense. Use safety bars or a spotter for heavy barbell exercises, keep your technique clean and stop when something hurts. In doubt about your health? Talk to a doctor first.</string>
